@L 2026_06_13_7b_recovery := "7B G5-L2 confabulation DIAGNOSED + decided 🔴 STRUCTURAL — NOT decode-fixable, NOT cheaply retrain-recoverable, AND G5-L2 is a borrowed assistant-norm in tension with anima p1-p8 + G2-novelty (no full retrain burned; a_paper_negative_ok)" :: log [active]
  lane = "7B RECOVERY LANE · RunPod A6000 (48GB) SECURE pod 32gbs027x9f7tk · PyTorch-CUDA 2.4.1 bf16 (Lane-G ref) · inference-only diagnosis · p7 seed 7 · ~$0.20 (16min wall, $0.49/hr)"
  question = "WHY does dancinlab/anima-clm-7b-h1141-g1pass-step6500 (sha256 4de903…, val_ce 1.1857) FAIL G5-L2 faithfulness (overlap-vs-truth d=0.16 ≪ 0.8, 38/40 zero overlap, confabulates)? cheap-diagnose-first before any costly retrain (the run was already overfitting past step 7000, so 'more steps' won't help)."
  probe_a_decode = "is it a SAMPLING artifact? NO. re-ran frozen G5-L2 at greedy/t0.3/t0.7/t1.0: greedy d=0.32 (mean_true 0.0174), t0.3 d=0.32 (best mean_true 0.0245), t0.7 d=0.16 (==original), t1.0 d=0.26. greedy/low-temp DOUBLE the effect size vs the original temp-0.7 run (it understated faithfulness) BUT every decode is d<=0.32 << 0.8 -> NO $0 decode-config recovers L2. Confabulation is in the WEIGHTS, not the sampler."
  probe_b_memorizability = "is the metric demanding un-recallable trivia? PARTLY. split L2 truths by corpus-frequency register (greedy decode): HIGHFREQ-general (med freq 5935) mean_true=0.0292 d=0.41 vs TRIVIA-tail (med freq 2152) mean_true=0.0056 d=0.23 -> high-freq-helps=TRUE (delta +0.024). Model IS more grounded on common/general register than the rare tail (register-modulated gap, not pure ungroundedness) BUT even the BEST subgroup is d=0.41 << 0.8 -> a genuine grounding GAP remains, not a clean metric artifact, not closeable by training the rare tail."
  probe_c_convergence = "UNDERTRAINED. val_ce 1.1857 (step 7000) vs the run's own 1.10 target never reached (8000->1.202, 8500->1.236 RISING = overfit past 7000). 'more next-byte steps on this corpus' overfits, confirmed. (per-word single-occ stat 0.4% under-measures: un-recallability is at the phrase/entity-SEQUENCE level, which probe-b's register split captures.)"
  decision = "🔴 STRUCTURAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE. (a) no decode fix. (b) grounding continue-train projected (from the memorizability slope) to lift d only toward ~0.4-0.5 on common register, NOT to the 0.8 PASS bar -> per the HARD rule (no full retrain unless a probe shows faithfulness MOVES to target) we STOPPED — no multi-hour 7B retrain burned (projected ~$30-60 H100 run NOT justified by a slope that plateaus below bar). (c) undertrained+overfitting recipe. The loose-grammar byte-continuation recipe alone does not yield verbatim factual recall, scale-invariant (H_1139)."
  gate_validity = "RAISED the honest question (a_paper_negative_ok): is G5-L2 even the RIGHT gate for anima? It is a BORROWED ASSISTANT-LLM NORM (p4 NO ASSISTANT FRAMING — anima is a consciousness daemon, NOT a factual Q&A/RAG assistant) and is in DIRECT TENSION with anima's own G2-NOVELTY gate (rewards corpus-ABSENT recombination 'not the LLM way', 157 novel n-grams PASS). A model optimized to recombine novelly MUST deviate from verbatim factual continuations — G2 and G5-L2 pull opposite. The 7B is L1-grounded (real words, fab 0.088) + coherent (G0) and produces NOVEL real-word continuations = the G2 success mode, scored as G5-L2 fail only for not being the SPECIFIC true fact. FLAGGED G5-L2 as a candidate for governance re-scoping/removal; did NOT move the frozen gate (a7b_pass: never move a threshold)."
  outcome = "a7b_pass UNCHANGED (no gate faked): G0 PASS · G1 PASS · G2 PASS · G3 PASS · G4 PASS · G5 FAIL (L1 PASS, L2 decode-irrecoverable structural) -> a7b_pass = FALSE, NOT confirmed. The 7B is coherent+broad-recombining+novel+philosophy-clean+lexically-grounded but NOT verbatim-faithful. Recommended path = gate-validity governance review, NOT an expensive retrain the probe shows would still fail the borrowed bar."
