@L 2026_06_13_h1200 := "MITOSIS-GENERATIVE-GROWTH 🔴 CLOSED-NEG — growth made next-byte generation WORSE (opposite direction): adding a per-cell next-byte head to the H_1199 VAdaptField and growing cells does NOT lower next-byte CE; pure-mitosis->chat falsified cheaply at the FIRST link (a_paper_negative_ok)" :: log [active]
  lane = "MITOSIS-ENGINE Lane-2 · FIRST rung of the 'can mitosis-growth reach conversational language?' arc · $0 local CPU numpy mirror · gradient-free p8 · 5 seeds"
  question = "The mitosis engine GROWS cells + lowers L2 RECON error (H_1198/H_1199 GREEN) — is that LANGUAGE-learning or just CLUSTERING? Give each grown prototype cell a GENERATIVE next-byte head (nearest-cell(context) -> that cell's online next-byte counts -> predict next byte) and test: does growing cells lower held-out next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY below a frozen-1-cell control (one global next-byte table)?"
  result = "🔴 CLOSED-NEG, F1 FAIL DECISIVELY in the WRONG direction: mitosis-ON next-byte CE 6.9930 > OFF CE 6.2352 => delta -0.7578 b/byte (bar +0.30) on EVERY one of 5 seeds. ON grows 1->~170 cells. F2 PASS (Spearman(n_cells,-CE)=+0.85, CE falls WITHIN the ON run as data accumulates) but does NOT rescue F1."
  mechanism = "COUNT-FRAGMENTATION: splitting fragments next-byte counts across ~170 cells (~14 samples/cell, smeared toward uniform by Laplace) while the single OFF table sees ALL data so it is sharper than any grown cell. The DIM=8 byte-feature key the cells cluster on identifies the local REGIME (latin/cjk/digits) but does NOT localise the NEXT byte enough to offset the data-split cost. F2's within-ON fall is a RED HERRING (more data by later blocks, not growth-beats-no-growth) — the F1 ON-vs-OFF test shows growth LOSES to one fat table. DECODE SAMPLES corroborate: GROWN greedy collapses to a degenerate repeated fragment, FROZEN greedy emits the most-common byte (space) — neither coherent; a DIM=8-feature-keyed gradient-free prototype-LM cannot generate text REGARDLESS of growth, and growth makes it WORSE."
  closes_gap = "the naive 'grow prototype cells -> they become a language model' path is FALSIFIED cheaply ($0). Mitosis-growth as built (H_1194..H_1199) is a CLUSTERING / reconstruction homeostat, NOT a generative LM — the growth->generation LINK is BROKEN at the first link. REDIRECT: generation belongs to the CLM lane (a_clm_gen_pipeline — a real ConvMoE next-byte head trained by descent); mitosis-growth is a structural/adaptation lane, not a generative-LM lane. The arc is saved from chasing a dead path."
  honesty = "FROZEN before scoring (freeze file pre-run; no threshold moved). NUMPY MIRROR of the H_1199 VAdaptField (mechanism VERBATIM: L2 nearest, recon-err>0.30 split, LR=0.20) + a NEW per-cell next-byte head; the live .hexa engine NOT edited (F3 Ψ-intact deferred to the .hexa-lift next rung honestly, NOT claimed — would only matter on a GREEN warranting the lift). DIM=8 window = COARSE context (no within-window token order) so absolute CE ~6-7 b/byte is far from a real LM; the falsifier is the ON-vs-OFF DELTA under the same coarse context. toy/small real-corpus FIRST rung, ONE corpus, 5 seeds; scale + conversational coherence UNVERIFIED — tests ONLY the growth->generation LINK, NOT chat (a_scale_honest_scope). p7 (CE = capability probe paired with verbatim decoded samples, NOT a chat/consciousness verdict)."
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1200_mitosis_generative_growth.py · .verdicts/1200_mitosis_generative_growth/H_1200_FREEZE.txt · .verdicts/1200_mitosis_generative_growth/H_1200.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md §h1200 · /tmp/h1200_result.json"

@L 2026_06_13_h1201 := "MITOSIS-CONDITIONED-GENERATION 🔴 CLOSED-NEG — mitosis is PURE SUBSTRATE for generation: conditioning a REAL gradient-trained next-byte head on the frozen mitosis cell-state does NOT beat the same head without it (gain NEGATIVE every seed); generation is CLM-only. Completes the H_1200 closure (mitosis can neither generate by itself NOR inform a real generator) — mitosis runs alongside as the adaptation/structural lane, CLM is the generator (a_clm_gen_pipeline, a_paper_negative_ok)" :: log [active]
  lane = "MITOSIS-ENGINE Lane-2 · the architecture-settling rung after H_1200 falsified pure-mitosis-as-LM · $0 summer CPU (numpy-MLP + real Adam, H_1192 precedent) · gradient-free mitosis (p8: only the readout head descends) · 3 seeds · English-wiki corpus /tmp/h1142/corpus_en.bin (byte-identical to the H_1129/H_1141 head)"
  question = "H_1200 (🔴) killed mitosis GENERATING by itself. OPEN: does the mitosis CELL-STATE carry information a REAL gradient-trained generative head can USE — does CONDITIONING a proper next-byte head on the frozen mitosis substrate BEAT the SAME head without it? If yes mitosis stays in the generation loop; if no mitosis is pure substrate and generation is CLM-only."
  method = "THREE heads IDENTICAL except input (same arch in->tanh(64)->softmax(256) + init seed + Adam lr3e-3 12ep batch256 + data + epochs — the whole validity of the test): BASELINE = DIM=8 H_1163 byte_feature (VERBATIM); CONDITIONED = same features ++ a +11-dim FROZEN mitosis summary from the H_1199 VAdaptField growth (gradient-free p8: nearest-proto[8] + recon-err + local density + log n_cells; read BEFORE pos i's own split, no leak); SHUFFLED = CONDITIONED with mitosis rows permuted (alignment destroyed; F2 capacity control, same width). N_TRAIN=12000 N_VAL=3000 contiguous, 3 seeds [900,901,902]. FROZEN F1 cond CE < base CE by >=0.05 b/byte; F2 shuffled keeps <0.5 of the gain (gain is INFO not capacity)."
  result = "🔴 CLOSED-NEG. F1 FAIL on the wrong side of zero: mean gain = -0.0206 b/byte (bar +0.05), NEGATIVE every seed (-0.0272/-0.0135/-0.0212); BASELINE CE 4.7006 < CONDITIONED 4.7213. F2 FAIL/moot: SHUFFLED CE 4.7307 WORSE still (keep_frac 1.459) — no positive gain to ablate, both conditioning arms only add noise. cells grew 1->{351,397,438}. DECODE: BASELINE + CONDITIONED greedy continuations BOTH degenerate ('o'/space repeats), conditioning changes nothing."
  mechanism = "the mitosis conditioning (nearest-prototype, recon-err, density) is a DETERMINISTIC LOSSY FUNCTION of the SAME byte-feature window the baseline already sees — it cannot add information the head does not already have, only redundancy/noise that mildly hurts via extra input dims. So mitosis-state is not a generation-useful signal for a feature-keyed head."
  closes_gap = "MITOSIS = PURE SUBSTRATE FOR GENERATION. Completes the two-rung closure: H_1200 🔴 (mitosis cannot GENERATE by itself) + H_1201 🔴 (mitosis cannot even INFORM a real generator) => the mitosis substrate is removed from the language-generation path ENTIRELY. Generation is CLM-only: 'conversational level' = pure CLM-lane scale-up (a_clm_gen_pipeline, a real ConvMoE next-byte head trained by descent); the mitosis engine (H_1194..H_1199) runs ALONGSIDE as the adaptation/structural/clustering lane. Decision-grade architecture ruling: mitosis=substrate, CLM=generator. a_paper_negative_ok."
  honesty = "FROZEN before scoring (freeze file pre-run; NO threshold moved). All arms IDENTICAL except input (F2 shuffle controls the extra width). Mitosis growth GRADIENT-FREE (p8: only the head descends — numpy MIRROR of the H_1199 VAdaptField; live .hexa engine NOT edited; the .hexa generative-conditioning lift F3-guarded Ψ-intact is the NEXT rung, NOT claimed a_core_engine_map). p7: CE = capability LINK probe paired with verbatim decoded samples, NOT a chat/consciousness verdict. NOT RULED OUT (honest): a DIFFERENT conditioning summary exposing mitosis state NOT recoverable from the current window (cross-window trajectory / temporal cell-history / learned embedding), or a richer head (sequence model with token order), is UNTESTED — this rules out the AS-BUILT VAdaptField clustering state as a conditioning signal for a feature-keyed head, NOT every mitosis->generation coupling. toy/small real-corpus, small MLP head, ONE corpus, 3 seeds; chat-level coherence + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). $0 summer CPU, co-tenant rbfe-prod untouched."
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1201_mitosis_conditioned_generation.py · .verdicts/1201_mitosis_conditioned_generation/H_1201_FREEZE.txt · .verdicts/1201_mitosis_conditioned_generation/H_1201.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md §h1201 · /tmp/h1201_result.json"

