@L 2026_06_13_h1149 := "🟢 ConvMoE+RETRO MOUNTABLE — the H_1147 copy head rides the engine-mountable CLMConvMoE E2/L1 trunk, flips fabrication 1.0→0.0, AND the trunk still serializes to a decodable .clm v0.2 (axis-6 303M architecture gap CLOSED)" :: discovery [d=2026-06-13 verified]
  what = "axis-6 of the 303M campaign: the H_1147 RETRO head was validated on a BYTEGPT backbone (axis-4 anima-303M-RETRO) which is NOT engine-mountable; only a CLMConvMoE E2/L1 trunk serializes to a generator-L3 .clm v0.2 (a_clm_gen_pipeline). So 'fabrication-solved' (ByteGPT+RETRO) and 'engine-mountable' (ConvMoE) were two DIFFERENT models. $0 numpy CPU toy: build a tiny CLMConvMoE E2/L1 (embed→embed_conv→trunk.0[GroupNorm+conv]→MoE[router+2 experts]→norm_out→readout) + the H_1147 copy head + the H_1147 un-memorizable must-copy toy."
  result = "🟢 GREEN, F1∧F2. F1 fab-flip: VANILLA-CONVMOE 1.0000 → CONVMOE-RETRO 0.0000 (gap 1.0000 ≥ 0.40, both bars cleared). F2 serializability: the ConvMoE-RETRO TRUNK (head excluded) serialized to .clm v0.2 (46742 bytes, nblk=6, n_ext=11), clm_serialize_v2._assert_e2_l1 PASS + teeth (E=4 cfg raises), clm_decodable=True, verify_clm_v2 struct PASS; CONVMOE-RETRO no-anchor control collapses to fab 1.0000 (copy-not-recall: grounds ONLY with the anchor). NO-ANCHOR floor 1.0000 confirms un-memorizability."
  finding = "RETRO MOUNTS ON CONVMOE — the head attaches as an ADDITIONAL module on the final-position trunk state (mirrors the ByteGPT attachment) WITHOUT touching the E2/L1 trunk operators, and STILL flips fabrication. KEY architecture truth: the RETRO head params (Pq,Pk,Wg) have NO slot in clm_serialize_v2._BLOCK_ORDER/_EXT_ORDER (which fetch by fixed slot name) ⇒ they are NATURALLY EXCLUDED from the .clm; the trunk round-trips byte-exact, _assert_e2_l1 still passes, the engine decodes the trunk as usual. ⇒ The head lives OUTSIDE the serialized trunk; CORE/clm_decode.hexa has NO copy path, so AT THE ENGINE DECODE the anti-fabrication benefit is TRAIN-TIME/HOST-SIDE ONLY — to run grounding INSIDE the A⇄G engine an engine-side copy head must be added to clm_decode + the generator L3 slot (a_core_engine_map: a separate 2nd-order engine build, NOT done here). DECISION for the final anima: ByteGPT-RETRO = language-research model; ConvMoE-RETRO = the mountable PRODUCTION trunk (same head, same fab-flip, serializes clean) — the production anima trains the RETRO head on a ConvMoE backbone; the in-engine copy decode is a follow-on engine build."
  honest = "a_scale_honest_scope: toy D=32, byte-subset vocab, ORACLE ground-truth anchor (H_1147/H_1148 retrieval surrogate) — NOT 303M, NOT real noisy/wrong kosmos retrieval, NOT a coherence-first backbone. 1.0/0.0 saturation = mechanism EXISTENCE-PROOF + serializability proof, NOT an effect size. The serializer/verifier are the PRODUCTION CLM/model/clm_serialize_v2.py + verify_clm_v2.py (reused unmodified, already on main). p7 deterministic (argmax fab-rate + byte-level .clm structural parse), NOT perplexity/LLM-judge. $0 local Mac CPU, no torch, no pod, no GPU — aiden/summer GPU (axis-1/3/4) + rbfe untouched."
